# A network of chips: this controller and two workers (worker.ic10), passing work
# through each other's memory. The controller puts a job into each worker's stack,
# then waits, a yield at a time, until both have answered. Each worker puts its
# result into this chip's stack, and beside it the job it answered (its
# acknowledgement):
#   stack[1] workerA's result   stack[3] the job workerA answered
#   stack[2] workerB's result   stack[4] the job workerB answered
# Things to try:
# - Breakpoint on "get ResultA": it stops once a round, when both have answered.
# - Breakpoint on "bne AckA Job wait" and Step Tick: watch the acknowledgements
#   (inline values) catch up. workerA answers first; workerB takes longer.
# - Variables, Stack: right-click "4 (above sp)", Break on Value Change. It
#   stops in workerB, after the put that acknowledged its job.
# - Variables, World on a worker's thread shows when its sleep ends.
alias WorkerA d0
alias WorkerB d1
alias Job r0
alias ResultA r1
alias ResultB r2
alias Total r3
alias JobB r4
alias AckA r5
alias AckB r6
move Job 0
loop:
add Job Job 1
put WorkerA 0 Job # workerA's job, in its stack
mul JobB Job 10
put WorkerB 0 JobB # workerB's is ten times bigger
wait:
yield
get AckA db 3 # the job workerA last answered
get AckB db 4
bne AckA Job wait # not this round's job yet: wait another tick
bne AckB JobB wait
get ResultA db 1 # both have answered: their results are here
get ResultB db 2
add Total ResultA ResultB
s db Setting Total
j loop
